00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.000
So what is the target of recall

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:11.000
Recall basically focuses on how much information of coverage

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
It can bring at one time

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.000
Out of the total information

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.000
So for coverage, some components are responsible

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.000
First is your embedding model

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.000
So you know that if your recall is less

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.000
Then you have to improve the embedding model

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.000
Second is your top case

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.000
If your top case is less

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.000
Then you have to increase the amount of retrieved chunks

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:39.000
And in some cases, chunk size can also be responsible

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.000
Although not in all cases

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.000
But these are the three hyper parameters

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:48.000
Which you keep in focus if your recall is less

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.000
If your precision is less

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:55.000
Means everything is retrieved and relevant retrieving is happening

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.000
But its order is not right

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:01.000
So here you will focus on reranker

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:06.000
You can put a specialized reranker in your rag pipeline

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.000
If the precision is less

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.000
Or it can be that if you are already using a reranker

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.000
Then tweak its settings

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.000
Refine it more

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.000
Third is your contextual relevancy

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:25.000
Contextual relevancy

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.000
This is your signal to noise ratio

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.000
So it focuses on three things

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.000
First it focuses on your top case

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.000
So by decreasing the top case

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Your noise decreases

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.000
Irrelevant chunks are no longer available

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.000
Second is your chunk size

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.000
If you reduce the chunk size

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.000
Then you can discard the noisy information

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.000
And third is your chunk overlap

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.000
By tweaking these parameters

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:58.000
You can increase your relevancy

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.000
Then comes your generator based matrix

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.000
Which has your answer relevancy

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:11.000
Answer relevancy basically focuses on your prompt

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:21.000
How your LLM is able to follow your input prompt or instructions

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
That is your answer relevancy

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
Already it has your query

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.000
What it has to do is to formulate the correct answer

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.000
So this is on the basis of your instruction

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:36.000
And fifth is your faithfulness or groundedness

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.000
This focuses on your prompt

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:45.000
But moreover it focuses on your LLM

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:51.000
That your LLM is showing the property of in-context learning

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.000
